# The Dockerfile never COPYs a secret, but that is only half the guarantee: the build context
# is tarred and uploaded to whatever builder runs the build (Fly's remote builder, a CI
# runner), so anything not excluded here leaves this machine even when it never lands in a
# layer. ADR-0014 §1's rule is that a key exists in as few places as possible; a credential
# sitting in a build context on someone else's machine is one of those places.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Not secrets, just weight and staleness. node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the
# build, and dist/ is rebuilt by `npm run build`; shipping the host's copies makes the build
# slower and lets a stale local artifact silently win over a fresh compile.
node_modules
dist
apps/*/dist
packages/*/dist
**/node_modules

.git
.github
.claude
supabase
.DS_Store
*.log
*.log.tmp
.scratch
.windkeel

# Documentation and research: several megabytes that no build step reads.
docs
research
bench
test
